// **`Pattern` and `Match` are `Comparable`.**
//
// `Match::cmp_value` orders by `(start, end, text)` — total over matches, which is what makes a
// `List<Match>` sortable — and `Pattern::cmp_value` orders by source, the same total order
// `key_capable: true` already promises so a pattern can key a map. A type that can key a map and
// cannot sort is the asymmetry this pins shut.
// expect: stdout "true"
// expect: stdout "true"
// expect: stdout "true"
// expect: stdout "true"
// expect: stdout "true"
// expect: exit 0
use std.{regex}

p = regex.compile('\d+')
all = p.find_all("a1b22c333")

// Matches come out in position order, and that is the order they compare in.
echo all[0] < all[1]
echo all.sorted().first() == some(all[0])
echo all.min() == some(all[0])
echo all.max() == some(all[2])

// A pattern's ordering is its source's — the same relation that lets it key a map.
q = regex.compile('a')
echo (p < q) == (p.source() < q.source())
